SECOND USE, ADDED 2026-09-09: THE WEBFONT ITSELF.

`public/fonts/inter-latin.woff2` and `public/fonts/inter-latin-ext.woff2` are
Inter as a font file, redistributed with this project.

Until now the interface set itself in Inter over a `<link>` to Google Fonts, so
no file was ours to redistribute. That link was removed: three render-blocking
stylesheets on an origin the browser had never resolved sat in front of the
first paint, and a public map that references `fonts.gstatic.com` sends every
visitor's IP to Google before they have consented to anything (CJUE, 2022).

Source: https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300..600&display=swap
        the two woff2 faces that answer names, latin and latin-ext,
        retrieved 2026-09-09 by `npm run fonts:build`.

WHAT WAS CHANGED. Nothing. The files are Google's own woff2 builds, byte for
byte as served; only the `src:` URL in the stylesheet points here instead of
there. The variable weight axis (300-600) is Google's subsetting, not ours.

OFL 1.1 permits this redistribution as part of a larger work. The reserved-font
-name clause (§5) is not engaged: the font is not modified, and it is served
under its own name. The paragraph above headed NO FONT FILE IS REDISTRIBUTED
describes the glyph-outline vendoring in `addressMarkerIcons.js` and remains
true of it — this section is the other, separate use.
